      "date": "Mon, 17 Aug 2026 09:04:59 IST",
      "content": "News Hoymiles Deploys 350 kW String Inverters in Bihar Under PM-KUSUM The 7.7 MW project uses 20 HINV350HX-G2 string inverters, each with a rated capacity of 350 kW, the company said in a statement while talking about the project. Manish Kumar 17 Aug 2026 09:47 IST Follow Us Hoymiles Deploys 350 kW String Inverters in Bihar Under PM-KUSUM Photograph: (Hoymiles) Global energy solutions company Hoymiles has commissioned a 7.7 MW solar power project in Gaya, Bihar, deploying 20 units of its 350 kW HINV350HX-G2 string inverters in what the company describes as its first project under the PM-KUSUM initiative in the area. Advertisment The project was executed by Naw Dharam Energy as the EPC partner, while Sun Solista served as the distribution partner for Hoymiles' inverter supply. The plant is set to dispatch green energy from the ground-mounted project to the local grid.. Advertisment The commissioning is significant for Hoymiles' India strategy as the company has traditionally been more closely associated with microinverter technology but has been expanding its portfolio in the country to include utility-scale string inverters, hybrid inverters and battery energy storage systems. 20 string inverters deployed The 7.7 MW project uses 20 HINV350HX-G2 string inverters, each with a rated capacity of 350 kW. According to Hoymiles, the inverter incorporates six 75-amp maximum power point trackers (MPPTs) and is compatible with both 182 mm and 210 mm photovoltaic modules. The company claims a maximum efficiency of 99.05% and European efficiency of 98.8%. Advertisment The HINV350HX-G2 is also designed for outdoor utility-scale applications, with IP66 protection and C5 anti-corrosion capability. The inverter has an SCR of ≥1.1, aimed at supporting stable operation under challenging grid conditions The choice of a 350 kW string inverter platform for the Gaya project reflects the growing deployment of high-capacity string inverters in utility-scale solar, where developers are seeking greater design flexibility while retaining relatively granular power-conversion architecture. Advertisment Hoymiles Expanding Portfolio Hoymiles' expansion in India is increasingly extending into energy storage alongside its established microinverter business. Advertisment In February, the company introduced its HOYDC 5MWh containerised BESS, targeting utility-scale and C&I applications. The system uses liquid cooling, integrated safety systems and a modular architecture designed for applications including renewable-energy integration, peak shaving, load shifting and grid support. The broader portfolio reflects Hoymiles' positioning as a solar and storage technology provider rather than a microinverter-only company. Its product portfolio now spans residential, C&I and utility applications, including microinverters, hybrid inverters and energy-storage solutions. Bihar PM-KUSUM Advertisment Read the Next Article",
