      "title": "Sherghati-Kajree rail link gets Railway ministry nod; ₹2627 cr project to connect Bihar and Palamu",
      "url": "https://thejharkhandstory.co.in/sherghati-kajree-rail-link-gets-railway-ministry-nod-₹2627-cr-project-to-connect-bihar-and-palamu/",
      "date": "Mon, 17 Aug 2026 00:48:01 IST",
      "content": "Breaking A ☀ ☽ Sherghati-Kajree rail link gets Railway ministry nod; ₹2,627 cr project to connect Bihar and Palamu THE JHARKHAND STORY NETWORK Daltonganj, August 16: The long-pending demand for a broad gauge railway line connecting Sherghati in Bihar’s Gaya district… August 16, 2026 · 3 min read Share WhatsApp X Facebook Copy link Vishnu Dayal Ram THE JHARKHAND STORY NETWORK Daltonganj, August 16: The long-pending demand for a broad gauge railway line connecting Sherghati in Bihar’s Gaya district with Kajree in Jharkhand’s Palamu district has moved a major step forward, with the Railway Ministry issuing a sanction memorandum for the 107.89-km project. The sanction memorandum, dated August 13, was issued by the Construction Organisation of East Central Railway. A copy of the document is available with . ₹2,627 Crore Railway Project According to the sanction memorandum, the project has an estimated cost of ₹2,627.29 crore. Three major railway departments—Civil Engineering, Signal and Telecommunication, and Electrical—will be involved in executing the project. Stay informed. Get Jharkhand's top stories in your inbox. Free. No spam. Unsubscribe anytime. The Civil Engineering department has been allocated ₹2,399.38 crore, while ₹104.05 crore has been earmarked for Signal and Telecommunication works and ₹123.86 crore for electrical works. Palamu MP Says 40-Year-Old Demand Finally Moves Forward Palamu BJP MP Vishnu Dayal Ram, who shared the development late on August 15, said the railway line had been a long-standing demand of the region. Advertisement “It was our long-overdue demand. It took me my first two terms in Parliament, and I received the sanction memorandum only during my ongoing third term in the Lok Sabha,” Ram said. The MP said he had repeatedly raised the issue in Parliament, including during Zero Hour and under Rule 377. “I have lost count of how many times I raised the issue of the broad gauge railway line between Sherghati in Gaya and Kajree in Palamu on the floor of the Lok Sabha,” he said. Advertisement Ram also thanked Union Railway Minister Ashwini Vaishnaw for approving the project. ALSO READ: Latehar road accident: Six killed, including child, in Chandwa collision Rail Link Expected to Boost Trade and Employment The proposed railway line is expected to improve connectivity between the two regions and provide a boost to trade, business and the local economy. Ram described the project as “a line of hope and progress”, saying improved rail connectivity could create new avenues for employment and business opportunities. Railway sources said the new line would reduce the travel distance between Sherghati and Kajree, near Daltonganj, by around 70 km. Kajree railway station is located only about 7 km from Daltonganj railway station, making the proposed connectivity particularly significant for Palamu. Project May Take Around Three Years According to railway sources, the project could take around three years to complete, although the timeline will depend on several factors, particularly land acquisition. Ram said land acquisition would be the first major challenge before construction can begin. “The Railways will first have to acquire land. It is",
