      "content": "Who's Who This section offers in-depth profiles of the distinguished individuals holding the nation's most prestigious positions across the legislature, executive branch, and judiciary. Explore detailed profiles of the leaders who shape national policy, drive progress, and uphold the principles that define our country. This includes the President, Vice President, Prime Minister, Chief Ministers, Members of Parliament, Governors, and the Chief Justice of India, etc. President Smt. Droupadi Murmu Read More Vice-President Shri C. P. Radhakrishnan Read More Prime Minister Shri Narendra Modi Read More Council of Ministers Previous slide Next slide View Ministers Rajya Sabha Members The Rajya Sabha, India's upper house of Parliament, has up to 250 members-238 elected from States and Union Territories and 12 nominated by the President. It is a permanent body, with one-third of its members retiring every two years, each serving six-year terms. View Members Lok Sabha Members The Lok Sabha, India's lower house of Parliament, comprises representatives elected by direct vote based on universal adult suffrage. The Constitution permits up to 550 members: 530 from the States and 20 from Union Territories. Currently, it has 542 elected members. The Lok Sabha's term is five years, unless dissolved earlier. View Members Governors & Lt. Governors Previous slide Next slide View Governors Chief Ministers Previous slide Next slide View CM’s Members of Legislative Assembly View Members Members of Legislative Council View Members Judges of Supreme Court View Judges Chiefs of Armed Forces View Chiefs",
