      "title": "Centre approves ₹1,419 crore detailed estimate for Qadian-Beas railway line in Punjab's ...",
      "url": "https://swarajyamag.com/news-brief/centre-approves-1419-crore-detailed-estimate-for-qadian-beas-railway-line-in-punjabs-majha-region",
      "date": "Mon, 17 Aug 2026 10:07:59 IST",
      "content": "Centre approves ₹1,419 crore detailed estimate for Qadian-Beas railway line in Punjab's Majha region News Brief Centre Approves Rs 1,419 Crore Detailed Estimate For Qadian-Beas Railway Line In Punjab's Majha Region Arjun Brij Aug 17, 2026 | Updated 10:55 AM GMT+5:30 Save & read from anywhere! Bookmark stories for easy access on any device or the Swarajya app . Sign In Prefer Prefer MoS Railways Ravneet Singh Bittu (Pic Via PIB) The Centre has approved a detailed estimate of Rs 1,419. 05 crore for the new 39.68 km Qadian-Beas broad gauge railway line in Punjab, BJP leader and former Union minister of state for Railways, Ravneet Singh Bittu, announced on Sunday (16 August). The project would connect Qadian in Gurdaspur district with Beas in Amritsar district through a 39.68 km broad-gauge corridor, marking a major breakthrough for the Majha region after nearly a century of delays. Describing it as a major milestone for Punjab and a historic development for the Majha region, Bittu expressed his gratitude to Prime Minister Narendra Modi, Railway Minister Ashwini Vaishnaw and the Railway Board for taking the long-pending project forward. The Centre had formally revived the project in June 2026 at an estimated cost of around Rs 1,400 crore, with the latest Railway Board sanction placing the detailed estimate at Rs 1,419 crore. The project envisages the development of state-of-the-art railway infrastructure, including two crossing stations at Ghuman and Butala, eleven major bridges and 121 minor bridges, fifty-four Road Under Bridges (RUBs), modern signalling and telecommunication systems and deployment of Kavach, India's indigenous train collision avoidance system. The project will be executed by Northern Railway, bringing several areas of the Majha belt onto the railway network. The project was first approved during 1928–29 by the then North-Western Railway, and construction work had progressed substantially by the early 1930s. However, changing circumstances and subsequent planning priorities led to its discontinuation. Recognising its strategic and developmental significance, the project was revived under the Socially Desirable Rail Connectivity Programme and included in the supplementary Railway Budget 2010–11. Bittu emphasised his personal involvement in pushing for the project's defreezing during his tenure as Union minister. The proposed alignment will pass through the important towns and villages of Qadian, Dhapai, Ghuman, Butala, Sathiala and Beas. The railway line also holds strategic significance as an alternative corridor for the vital Amritsar–Pathankot section. Please click here to add Swarajya as your preferred and trusted news source on Google Also Read: Delhi's IGI Airport Announces Phased Expansion To Handle 125 Million Travellers By 2032 Arjun Brij is a Newsroom Associate at Swarajya. He tracks infrastructure and trade developments and posts on X at @arjun_brij. Tags Punjab Indian Railways Infrastructure Ravneet Singh Bittu Qadian-Beas Railway Join our WhatsApp channel - no spam, only sharp analysis Comments ↓ Get Swarajya in your inbox. Subscribe States",
